{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "Dm66eqJVgO", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905465, "segment_id": "16WrGxCRLA", "segment_broadcast_id": "Dm66eqJVgO", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Katie Couric (New York)", "segment_description": null, "segment_duration": 60, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905465, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Dm66eqJVgO", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905465, "segment_id": "Cs47BqfvAr", "segment_broadcast_id": "Dm66eqJVgO", "segment_title": "Economy: Rescue Plan", "segment_description": "(Studio: Katie Couric)  The reaction of the stock market to the government bailout plan for the troubled economy and the record jump in oil prices noted; Stock Market Report.  \n\n(Washington: Bob Orr)  The 700-billion dollar bailout plan examined; details given of the issues of capping executive compensation, mortgage relief, an oversight board and shares in the aided companies for the government.  [Senator Christopher DODD&nbsp- raises caution.]  [Representative Barney FRANK&nbsp- offers a view on the plan.]  Statement from President Bush calling for quick passage quoted.  \n\n(Studio: Katie Couric)  Report introduced.  \n\n(New York: Anthony Mason)  The reaction of the financial markets to the plan examined.  [Seaport Securities Corp. Ted WEISBERG&#134;- calls for transparency.]  [Ladenburg Thalmann and Co. Richard BOVE&#134;- cites the reason for the tumble in stocks.]  The announcement by Goldman Sachs and MorganStanley they are remaking themselves as commercial banks and the fall of bank stocks noted.  [Egan-Jones Ratings Co. Sean EGAN&#134;- cites the risks for Washington Mutual.]  The record jump in oil prices today discussed. ", "segment_duration": 320, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63060.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905466, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Dm66eqJVgO", "broadcast_date": "2008-09-22", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1730, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 905465, "segment_id": "Om5uGNW4l4", "segment_broadcast_id": "Dm66eqJVgO", "segment_title": "Campaign 2008 / Obama vs. McCain / Financial Issue", "segment_description": "(Studio: Katie Couric)  Report introduced.   (Media, Pennsylvania: Chip Reid)  The response of presidential candidates Senator Barack Obama and Senator John McCain to the government's bailout plan featured; details given about their common ground and the criticism and counter-criticism.  [OBAMA&nbsp- says we cannot give a blank check to Washington; calls for a plan for relief for hard-working Americans.]  [McCAIN&nbsp- says the plan makes him uncomfortable; wants to keep people in their homes and protect the financial system.]   (Studio: Katie Couric)  The early voting in three states noted; Pew Center map shown of states with in-person early voting. ", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63380.0", "legacy_segment_id": 905467, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_